ARTIFACTS ARE A SEPARATE QUESTION, AND AN OPEN ONE

The Apache-2.0 grant above is over this repository's code and documents.

Whether it reaches the artifacts is not settled, and this file does not settle
it. The question is whether a steering vector is a derivative work of the model
its activations were read from, and there is a real case on both sides.

Against: a direction is something its author built. They wrote the contrast
prompts, chose the layer and the estimator, and did arithmetic on activations
they elicited. The result contains no weights, cannot reconstruct any, and is
better described as a measurement of a model than a piece of one. On that
reading the author holds whatever rights exist and grants them here.

For: the numbers are a function of the weights, and some model licenses define
derivative works broadly enough to reach things computed from them.

Nobody has litigated it, and whether model weights attract copyright at all is
itself contested. So: the author licenses what is his under Apache-2.0, and a
reader who wants to redistribute an artifact should read the source model's
license themselves rather than rely on this file. `CLAUDE.md` states the
working rule as "redistributing one **may be** constrained", and that hedge is
deliberate.

What this repository actually holds, as of 2026-09-19:

  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_v1.safetensors
  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_logistic.safetensors
  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_lda.safetensors
  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_L24_logistic.safetensors

      Directions read out of allenai/Olmo-3-1125-32B, which is Apache-2.0,
      Extracted by the author from github.com/soham-padia/steering-arena at
      commit b8b4721. See artifacts/REAL.md.

  fixtures/*.safetensors

      Synthetic. Integer ramps written by fixtures/build.py against model ids
      that resolve to nothing. Not derived from any model, and every number
      attached to them is invented and labeled as such. See
      fixtures/SYNTHETIC.md.

One artifact in the corpus is not in this repository:

  soham/meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct/trauma@d61-diffmeans-expository-L34

      Read out of meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct, which is the Llama 3.3
      Community License and is NOT Apache-2.0. Those bytes are published in
      the author's own Hugging Face namespace and this repository records only
      a pointer to them. Its row carries the author's dated reading of that
      license, including a clause he records as unresolved: whether the
      requirement to begin a derivative model's name with "Llama" reaches a
      read-out direction vector is not settled by the text.

The registry points at artifacts and serves none. A pointer is not a
redistribution, which is why the Llama-derived direction can be indexed here
while its bytes stay where their author put them, and why the open
question above is less urgent here than it would be for a host.
